{
  "an8.24:0.1": "Numbered Discourses 8.24 ",
  "an8.24:0.2": "3. Householders ",
  "an8.24:0.3": "With Hatthaka (2nd) ",
  "an8.24:1.1": "At one time the Buddha was staying near Āḷavī, at Āḷavī’s premier shrine. ",
  "an8.24:1.2": "Then the householder Hatthaka of Āḷavī, escorted by around five hundred lay followers, went up to the Buddha, bowed, and sat down to one side. The Buddha said to Hatthaka: ",
  "an8.24:1.3": "“Hatthaka, you have a large congregation. ",
  "an8.24:1.4": "How do you bring together such a large congregation?” ",
  "an8.24:1.5": "“Sir, I bring together such a large congregation by using the four ways of being inclusive as taught by the Buddha. ",
  "an8.24:1.6": "When I know that they ",
  "an8.24:1.7": "can be included by a gift, I include them by giving a gift. ",
  "an8.24:1.8": "When I know that they ",
  "an8.24:1.9": "can be included by kindly words, I include them by kindly words. ",
  "an8.24:1.10": "When I know that they ",
  "an8.24:1.11": "can be included by taking care of them, I include them by caring for them. ",
  "an8.24:1.12": "When I know that they ",
  "an8.24:1.13": "can be included by equality, I include them by treating them equally. ",
  "an8.24:1.14": "But also, worthy sir, my family is wealthy. ",
  "an8.24:1.15": "They wouldn’t think that a poor person was worth listening to in the same way.” ",
  "an8.24:1.16": "“Good, good, Hatthaka! ",
  "an8.24:1.17": "This is the right way to bring together a large congregation. ",
  "an8.24:1.18